  "reason": "The current best is config_005 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) at 0.650 acc. For pca_n2000, avgpool clearly outperformed transformer (0.591 vs 0.519), but the optimal aggregation may differ for scvi_n200's learned latent representations. config_006 is a clean single-variable comparison (only aggregation changes from avgpool to transformer) that directly tests whether transformer aggregation could unlock further gains with the best-performing encoder. This is the highest-value exploitation step: it either confirms avgpool as the correct aggregation (freeing the remaining 3 experiments to explore multimodal fusion with scvi_n200) or discovers a new best configuration to build upon. Given the weak image-only signal (0.208), solidifying the RNA-only ceiling before adding a second modality is the prudent use of this experiment."
}

